摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Local-first, self-hosted AI agent runtime and MCP bridge with sandboxed sessions, memory, credentials, audit/replay, and a local Console.","id":"gh:1297278222","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"sandbase-harness","slug":"sandbaseai/sandbase-harness","topics":["agent-harness","agent-observability","agent-plugin","agent-runtime","agent-sandbox","ai-agents","ai-infrastructure","audit-logging","deepseek-harness","devops","docker","dsh-plugin","harness-engineering","kubernetes","local-first","mcp-gateway","mcp-server","model-context-protocol","sandboxed-execution","self-hosted"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Local-first, self-hosted AI agent runtime and MCP bridge with sandboxed sessions, memory, credential"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"s, audit/replay, and a local Console."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# SandBase Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"AI-readable project metadata: llms.txt · installation guide"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"A local-first runtime for AI agents. Sessions, sandboxed tools, memory,\ncredentials, audit trails, a"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"nd a built-in Console — all running on your\nmachine or in your own infrastructure."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Agent SDKs handle the model loop. Production agents need more: persistent\nsessions, tool governance,"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" sandbox boundaries, credential handling, memory,\nauditability, and a UI for humans to inspect what "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"happened. `managed-agents`\nis that runtime layer — not a visual workflow builder and not another mod"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"d. `managed-agents`\nis that runtime layer — not a visual workflow builder and not another model SDK."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| Need | What Harness provides |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Run generated code safely | Local, Docker, Kubernetes, and self-hosted worker sandboxes |\n| Inspec"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"t long-running agents | Persistent sessions, resumable event streams, audit, and replay |\n| Control "},{"id":"p9s3","text":"tool access | MCP toolsets, credential vaults, permission policies, and approvals |\n| Operate any mo"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"del | OpenAI, Anthropic, MiniMax, and OpenAI-compatible providers, including DeepSeek V4 |\n| Keep in"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"frastructure yours | Local-first SQLite and file storage with no required hosted control plane |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- Claude Managed Agents-style `/v1` API and local Console\n- SQLite metadata by default for agents, s"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"essions, environments, credential\nvaults, memory stores, files, skills, and API keys — local file/sk"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ill bytes\nin the workspace state directory\n- Resumable Server-Sent Events for session replay and deb"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"ugging\n- One active model provider boundary configured through Settings V2\n- Sandbox backends: local"},{"id":"p11s5","text":" process, Docker (per-session containers), Kubernetes\n(kubectl exec/cp), self-hosted worker queue\n- "},{"id":"p11s6","text":"MCP toolsets, permission policies, built-in tools, and skill packages\n- TypeScript SDK at `managed-a"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"gents/sdk`\n- Release gate: `npm run release:check`"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Quick Start"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Requirements: Node.js 22+, npm 10+, and a model provider API key (OpenAI,\nAnthropic, MiniMax, or any"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" OpenAI-compatible endpoint). Docker is optional and\nonly needed for Docker-backed sandboxes."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"`init` writes a workspace into the directory you run it from: an agent, a skills\nfolder, and `config"},{"id":"p15s2","text":".yaml`, whose provider reference is the `${OPENAI_API_KEY}`\nenvironment variable. `start` serves the"},{"id":"p15s3","text":" API and the Console on\n<http://127.0.0.1:3000>."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Two steps finish the setup, both on **Settings > Setup** at\n<http://127.0.0.1:3000/dashboard>:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"1. **The provider.** Paste your API key into the provider form and save. The page\nthen reports that "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"the saved configuration is not active yet, so restart the\nruntime — stop it with Ctrl+C and run the "},{"id":"p17s3","text":"`start` command again, or use the\nrestart button. A saved setting only takes effect at startup. If y"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"our provider\nis not in the list, choose the OpenAI-compatible vendor and set its base URL.\n2. **The "},{"id":"p17s5","text":"model.** In the **Agent models** panel, set the model ID your provider\nactually serves — `deepseek-c"},{"id":"p17s6","text":"hat` for DeepSeek, for example. An agent carries\nits own model ID, so the `gpt-4o` that `init` write"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"s is not valid for every\nprovider, and a wrong ID fails the turn with `model_not_found`."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Send the first message from the Console: open **Sessions**, create a session for\nthe agent, and type"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" into the composer. From a terminal it is one command:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"`chat` sends that one message and exits once the turn settles; without\n`--message` it keeps the sess"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ion open and streams until you interrupt it.\n`--tool-approval allow`\npreauthorizes the tool calls th"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"e agent may make, which the `init` template\notherwise parks for approval and waits for a person to a"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"e, which the `init` template\notherwise parks for approval and waits for a person to answer; see CLI."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The unscoped `managed-agents` name on npm is not this project. Until an\nofficial scoped package is a"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"nnounced in this repository, install only from the\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## CMA compatibility"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Coverage of the published Claude Managed Agents contract is declared entry by\nentry in `src/core/cap"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"abilities/matrix.ts`:\nof the official SDK's route surface (110 method/path pairs as of SDK\n`0.132.1`"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"), 90 routes are mounted and 20 refuse by name; no route is deferred.\n`Partial` and `Unsupported` en"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"tries always name their reason."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"The table below is generated by `npm run docs:compat`, and a contract-honesty\ntest fails when it dri"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"fts from the matrix."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Full compatibility table (generated)"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Area | Official capability | Status | Notes |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| headers | `compatibility-header-admission` | Partial | Version, beta, and mutual-exclusion rules a"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"re enforced for any request that carries a compatibility header. A request with no compatibility hea"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"der is accepted as a local caller, which the published contract does not define; this header-free pa"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"th is a deliberate local-first extension for a self-hosted single-tenant runtime, recorded as such i"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"n the headers contract §4, and it is why this entry stays partial. |\n| headers | `extension-namespac"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"e-exclusion` | Supported |  |\n| pagination | `opaque-cursors` | Partial | A collection's envelope fo"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"llows the mount: the operations router serves `/v1` with `{data, prev_page, next_page}` and its `/v1"},{"id":"p27s8","text":"/x` mirror with the local `{data, has_more, first_id, last_id}`, chosen through one pager so no hand"},{"id":"p27s9","text":"ler emits both spellings, and cursors that are readable base64url JSON rather than opaque binary. Ev"},{"id":"p27s10","text":"ery canonical `/v1` collection serves the canonical envelope, with no exceptions: the complete-set l"},{"id":"p27s11","text":"istings carry `{data, prev_page: null, next_page: null}` and the windowed ones carry a followable cu"},{"id":"p27s12","text":"rsor — `/v1/sessions` pages by number under `{order, created_at bounds, page}` and rejects a cursor "},{"id":"p27s13","text":"replayed under another ordering or creation window, `/v1/sessions/{id}/events` carries `{order, filt"},{"id":"p27s14","text":"er, after_id}`, `/v1/skills` and the credential audit listings use `{offset, filter}` — so a cut pag"},{"id":"p27s15","text":"e says so instead of looking complete. The one listing that is neither shape is `/v1/environments/{i"},{"id":"p27s16","text":"d}/work-items`, a windowed extension that adds a `counts` object and is named in the contract. |\n[该节"},{"id":"p27s17","text":"rk-items`, a windowed extension that adds a `counts` object and is named in the contract. |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
